      "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2017 the Syndicate had gross claims outstanding of GBP 210.466m. During 2017 cumulative gross ultimate claims movements (per the gross claims development table) produced a net adverse movement of approximately GBP 12.8m (gross strengthening) concentrated in several older underwriting years, while on a net-of-reinsurance basis the Syndicate reported an aggregate net reserve release of GBP 0.8m. The gross strengthening was driven by adverse development in parts of the Liability and Accident & Health portfolios (including two large Financial Institutions liability claims following the FCA annuity review), partially offset by favourable development / releases in the Property, Marine and Credit & Political Risk accounts. Major 2017 natural catastrophe activity (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma and Maria and California wildfires) influenced current year losses and reinsurance placements but reinsurance recoveries and reserve movements produced mixed impacts across lines.",
